hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1370","Bundar told us, Yahya told us, Ismail told us, Qais told me, on the authority of Abu Masoud Uqba bin Amr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “The sun and the moon do not eclipse due to the death of anyone, but they are two signs of God, so when you see them, pray.” Abu Bakr said: His statement: “When you see it, pray,” is an indication of the argument of the doctrine of al-Muzani, may God have mercy on him, in the issue with which he differed. In it, some of our companions took an oath if he had two wives, and he said: If you give birth to a son, you are both divorced. Al-Muzani said: If you give birth One of them has a child, and they are divorced, since it is known that two women do not give birth to one child together, but only one woman gives birth to one, so say The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When you see it, pray.” Rather, what he meant was: If you see the eclipse of one of them, pray, since knowledge is surrounding that the sun The moon does not eclipse at the same time, just as two women do not give birth to one child."
